+/* sidecar/run-override.js — A MODEL FOR ONE RUN ONLY (CA PHE DIGITAL, company/patches/0017).
+
+   WHY. A run's model was set seat-wide: the routine's saved pair, else the agent's roster pin. A caller that wanted one
+   item on a stronger (or cheaper) model had to re-pin the agent and put the pin back afterwards, and every other run on
+   that agent in between ran on the borrowed model too. POST /api/cron/run and each team.dispatch worker spec now take an
+   optional { model, provider, effort } that applies to THAT run only. Nothing saved changes: the routine keeps its own
+   pair and the agent keeps its pin. The run row says requestedBy:'override' and what was asked (runstore.js).
+
+   THE RULE.
+     - all three absent (or empty)  -> no override: the run resolves exactly as it did before this record.
+     - model                         -> a well-formed model id. Its shape is checked, not its presence in a catalog: a
+                                        provider's model list is not complete (the Claude CLI's curated list leaves Fable
+                                        out on purpose, claude-cli.js MODELS), and a model the provider does not serve
+                                        fails on that provider in its own words like any pinned model.
+     - provider                      -> a provider id this station's registry knows (normalizeProvider answers '' for
+                                        any other); a provider with no model is refused, as everywhere (a provider
+                                        names no model: run-wire.js). A bare model borrows the routine's provider
+                                        (Run Now), else the next level's, by the one run-wire rule.
+     - effort                        -> one of EFFORTS.
+   Anything else answers { ok:false, error } in plain words; the host sends it back as a 400 (Run Now) or as that
+   worker's error row (team.dispatch), and nothing runs.
+   A well-formed override still runs only when the company's override allowlist opens its resolved (provider, model)
+   for that run's own agent now (sidecar/override-allow.js, env STARNET_OVERRIDE_ALLOW): no current list -> 403 / the
+   worker's error row "no current override allowlist: overrides are off"; not listed -> "model p/m is not open for
+   <agentId> now". This module only parses; the gate is the host's (index.js handleCronRun, orchestration allowOverride).
+
+     parseRunOverride(spec, { normalizeProvider?, knownProviders? }) -> { ok:true, override: null | {provider?, model?, effort?} }
+                                                                     | { ok:false, error }
+     explicitOf(override, base)  -> the explicit level for run-wire.js resolveRunWire / index.js runWireFor: the override's
+                                    model (and provider, else base's provider when the override names only a model), the
+                                    override's effort; an effort-only override keeps base's pair at that effort.
+
+   UMD and dependency-free (the sidecar, orchestration and tests share it). */
+'use strict';
+(function (root, factory) {
+  const api = factory();
+  if (typeof module === 'object' && module.exports) module.exports = api;
+  else { root.SK = root.SK || {}; root.SK.runOverride = api; }
+})(typeof self !== 'undefined' ? self : this, function () {
